            <ArticleTitle>Surface-selective direct 17O DNP NMR of CeO2 nanoparticles.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2142-2145</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc10145c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Surface-selective direct 17O DNP has been demonstrated for the first time on CeO2 nanoparticles, for which the first three layers can be distinguished with high selectivity. Polarisation build-up curves show that the polarisation of the (sub-)surface sites builds up faster than the bulk, accounting for the remarkable surface selectivity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
